.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt BOSD.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bosd.conf
.Nd default options for the bosd on-screen display
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Pa @PREFIX@/etc/bosd.conf
supplies defaults for optional
.Xr bosd 1
flags.
.Ev BOSD_CONF ,
when set and not empty, names the file instead.
Each
.Nm bosd
process uses the value it inherited, so a daemon keeps the path it
was started with.
A missing file is valid: every default below is then the built-in
value, and
.Nm
does not create the file.
The sample, which lists those built-in values, is
.Pa @PREFIX@/share/examples/bosd/bosd.conf .
Copying that sample onto the path above does not change behavior.
.Pp
The format is one
.Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value
per line, which is what
.Cm sysconf generic
reads and writes:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sysconf generic -f @PREFIX@/etc/bosd.conf screen=eDP-1
.Ed
.Pp
A
.Ql #
starts a comment, through the end of the line, unless the
.Ql #
is inside quotes.
Blank lines are ignored.
A value is quoted only when it contains whitespace, a
.Ql # ,
a double quote, or a backslash.
Inside quotes,
.Ql \e
escapes the next character.
Names are case sensitive.
A later assignment of the same name wins.
An unknown name, or a value outside the range of the matching flag,
is an error and
.Nm bosd
exits without drawing.
A flag on the command line overrides the file.
.Pp
.Xr bosd 3
does not read this file.
A program that calls
.Fn bosd_show
sends the request it built.
.Sh SCREEN
.Sy screen
corresponds to
.Fl S .
Empty, or leaving the name unset, means the primary output,
or the built-in panel when no primary is set.
.Cm primary
does not use that fallback.
.Cm mouse
is the output under the pointer.
.Pp
.Nm bosd
started with
.Fl d
and without
.Fl S
adopts
.Sy screen
as the screen a later request uses when that request also omits
.Fl S .
A show handed to a running daemon without
.Fl S
does not itself name a screen, so the daemon's default stays in
force: that process's
.Fl S ,
or
.Sy screen
from the file, or the primary.
The daemon reads the file when it starts and on
.Dv SIGHUP .
.Fl S
on the daemon is not replaced by the file.
A broken file leaves the screen already in use.
.Pp
A local show
.Po
.Fl D ,
or no daemon on the channel
.Pc
without
.Fl S
uses
.Sy screen
from the file directly.
.Sh SETTINGS
Each name is the default for the flag in the description.
The value shown is the built-in used when the file is missing or
the name is omitted.
.Bl -tag -width "outline_alpha"
.It Sy screen
.Fl S .
Output name
.Pq such as DP-4 or eDP-1 ,
or
.Cm all ,
or
.Cm primary ,
or
.Cm mouse .
Empty selects the primary, or the built-in panel when no
primary is set.
.Cm primary
does not use that fallback.
.Cm mouse
is the output under the pointer.
See
.Sx SCREEN .
.It Sy alpha
.Fl A .
.Fl 1
leaves a PNG's own alpha alone
.Pq and is full opacity for text and the gauge .
Otherwise 0 to 1.
.It Sy outline_alpha
.Fl O .
Opacity of the outline, 0 to 1.
The built-in is 1.
This is not
.Sy alpha .
.It Sy outline
The inverse of
.Fl o .
.Cm yes
draws the outline
.Pq the built-in ;
.Cm no
is
.Fl o .
Also accepted:
.Cm on ,
.Cm off ,
.Cm true ,
.Cm false ,
.Cm 1 ,
and
.Cm 0 .
There is no flag that forces the outline back on, so
.Cm no
in the file is not overridden by omitting
.Fl o .
.It Sy font
.Fl f .
A fontconfig family.
Empty is DejaVu Sans, then Sans.
.It Sy text_color
.Fl F .
Name or
.Li #rrggbb
for
.Fl c ,
.Fl t ,
.Fl T ,
and
.Fl b
text, and for gauge labels.
Empty is green for
.Fl t
and white otherwise.
.It Sy gauge_color
.Fl G .
Fill of the
.Fl g
bar.
Empty is
.Li #2AC12A .
Does not itself draw a bar.
.It Sy scale
.Fl s .
Multiplier on the panel-derived size, 0.1 to 8.
The built-in is 1.
.It Sy x
.Fl x .
Pixels, positive right.
The built-in is 0.
.It Sy y
.Fl y .
Pixels, positive down.
The built-in is 0.
.It Sy hold
.Ar hold_seconds
for a glyph,
.Fl t ,
or
.Fl T
when that operand is omitted.
.Fl 1
holds until replaced or cleared; otherwise 0.01 to 30.
The built-in is 2.
An operand on the show replaces it.
.Fl c
keeps its own default of 1 second per digit unless that show
passes
.Ar hold_seconds .
This is not
.Sy gauge_hold .
.It Sy gauge_hold
.Fl B .
Seconds the bar stays up.
.Fl 1
holds until replaced or cleared; otherwise 0.01 to 30.
The built-in is 3.
Does not itself draw a bar.
.It Sy gauge_prev
.Fl P .
Prior-percent watermark.
.Fl 1
disables it
.Pq the built-in ;
otherwise 0 to 9999.
Does not itself draw a bar.
.El
.Pp
.Sy outline Ns = Ns Cm no
together with an
.Sy outline_alpha
other than 1 is rejected, the same as
.Fl o
with
.Fl O .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "@PREFIX@/share/examples/bosd/bosd.conf" -compact
.It Pa @PREFIX@/etc/bosd.conf
defaults when
.Ev BOSD_CONF
is unset or empty; missing is valid
.It Pa @PREFIX@/share/examples/bosd/bosd.conf
sample, set to the built-in values
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bosd 1 ,
.Xr sysconf 8 ,
.Xr sysconf-generic 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Devin Teske Aq Mt dteske@FreeBSD.org
